        "original_id": "0ddd48a1-ebc0-5178-ac22-33168039c1db",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Rickenbacker Air National Guard Base, Lockbourne, Franklin County, Columbus\n- Organizations: Ohio Air National Guard\n- People: Eddie Rickenbacker\n- Topics: Air National Guard facilities, World War I, Medal of Honor\n\nFacts:\n- Edward Vernon Rickenbacker was born on October 8, 1890, and he was an American fighter ace in World War I.\n- Edward Vernon Rickenbacker was a Medal of Honor recipient.\n- Rickenbacker Air National Guard Base has operated from 1942 to the present.\n- Rickenbacker Air National Guard Base is an Air National Guard facility of the Ohio Air National Guard.\n- Rickenbacker Air National Guard Base is located near Lockbourne in southern Franklin County.\n- Rickenbacker Air National Guard Base was named for Eddie Rickenbacker, an early aviator and Columbus native.\n- Edward Vernon Rickenbacker died on July 23, 1973.",
